---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Record HTTP(S) traffic through a local proxy; manage its local CA

Usage: rustman record [OPTIONS]
       rustman record <COMMAND>

Commands:
  ca    Manage this workspace's local CA, used to decrypt intercepted hosts
  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --host <HOST>
          Address to bind: an IP address or localhost (default: [record] host in rustman.toml, else 127.0.0.1)

      --port <PORT>
          Port to bind; 0 picks a free port (default: [record] port in rustman.toml, else 8888)

      --allow-remote
          Allow binding an address reachable from the network (anyone who can reach it can use the proxy and see intercepted traffic)

      --intercept <GLOB>
          Decrypt HTTPS to hosts matching GLOB with the local CA (repeatable; default: [record] intercept); other hosts stay opaque tunnels

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace whose settings and CA to use (default: search from the current directory upwards; recording without interception works without one)

      --include-host <GLOB>
          Record only hosts matching GLOB (repeatable)

      --exclude-host <GLOB>
          Do not record hosts matching GLOB (repeatable)

      --method <METHOD>
          Record only this method (repeatable)

      --content-type <PREFIX>
          Record only exchanges whose request or response content type starts with PREFIX (repeatable)

      --keep-static
          Also record static assets (images, fonts, CSS, JavaScript, media, source maps), dropped by default

      --json
          Print one redacted JSON object per capture instead of a summary line

      --upstream <URL>
          Reverse-proxy mode: forward every request received to this origin (https://api.example.com), for clients that cannot use a proxy

      --insecure
          Do not verify the --upstream server's TLS certificate

      --save
          When recording stops (Ctrl+C), save the captures as request files

      --into <DIR>
          Folder for the saved request files (default: recorded/<host>/)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment that receives base_url, path defaults and secret names (default: recorded)

      --store-secrets
          Store the raw secret values in the secret store (keychain); without it they are kept nowhere and must be set with 'rustman secret set'

      --har <FILE>
          When recording stops (Ctrl+C), write every capture to FILE as HAR 1.2, secrets redacted

      --show-secrets
          Keep secret values in the --har file instead of redacting them

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
